IMPORT prelude

-- Copyright Act 2021 (Singapore) -- who is the FIRST OWNER of copyright: the default rule (s 133), works made by an employee in
-- the course of a contract of service (s 134), and the Government's ownership of works made under its direction or control
-- (s 136(1), (2)). The definitions used: "authorial work" (s 9), "literary work" includes a computer program (s 13(1)(b)),
-- "contract of service" (s 7(1), pointing to s 2(1) of the Employment Act 1968).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 9/3/2025" in the page footers), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CA2021.txt. Section numbers were read from the BODY (Part 3, Division 8 -- Ownership and
-- transactions, ss 133 to 136).
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0287 (Haziq scenario, event h045): software written by salaried engineers of a company in
-- the course of their employment, nothing in their contracts about ownership -- who owns the copyright?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: whether copyright subsists at all (qualified individuals, connecting factors, s 133(2) on joint authors who are not
-- qualified individuals); what counts as a "contract of service" (Employment Act 1968 s 2(1), not deposited here) and when a work is
-- made "in the course of" one (case law); commissioned photographs, portraits, engravings, sound recordings and films under
-- agreements made before 21 November 2021 (s 135); prescribed international organisations (s 136(3), (4)); s 136(1)(b) and (c)
-- (published works and editions first published by the Government); what the parties' contrary agreement actually provides (the
-- encoding only says the statutory default is displaced); assignment, licences and transmission (s 137 onward); moral rights and the
-- employment exceptions in Part 5.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Copyright Act 2021 -- first ownership`

§§ `9, 13 -- kinds of work`

-- s 9: "An 'authorial work' is a literary, dramatic, musical or an artistic work."
-- s 13(1): "A 'literary work' includes -- (a) a compilation in any form; and (b) a computer program."
-- s 13(3): a "computer program" is "an expression (in any language, code or notation) of a set of instructions ... intended to ...
-- cause a device with information processing capabilities to perform a particular function".
DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF
    `computer program`
    `literary work`
    `dramatic work`
    `musical work`
    `artistic work`
    `published edition`
    `sound recording`
    `film`
    `broadcast`
    `cable programme`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a literary work` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `computer program` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `literary work` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an authorial work` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `computer program` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `literary work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dramatic work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `musical work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `artistic work` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `the facts`

-- One record per work. Dates are taken as two flags, because the Act turns on two days only: 10 April 1987 (s 134(4)) and
-- 21 November 2021 (ss 133(3), 134(1)(b), 134(5), 136(2)).
DECLARE Making HAS
    `the kind of work` IS A Kind
    `made by an employee in the course of a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made on or after 21 November 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made on or after 10 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer is the proprietor of a periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made for publication in a periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by or under the direction or control of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `still unpublished when made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contrary agreement exists` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement was made on or after 21 November 2021` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `133(3), 134(5), 136(2) -- contrary agreement`

-- s 133(3): ss 133(1), (2) "are subject to any contrary intention in -- (a) any written agreement made on or after 21 November 2021
-- by the person who would otherwise be the first owner ...; or (b) any agreement before 21 November 2021 by" that person.
-- s 134(5): ss 134(3), (4) "are subject to any contrary intention in -- (a) any written agreement made between the employer and the
-- employee on or after 21 November 2021; or (b) any agreement made between the employer and the employee before 21 November 2021."
-- s 136(2) is in the same form for an agreement made by the Government.
-- So from 21 November 2021 only a WRITTEN agreement displaces the default; an earlier agreement may be oral.
-- (The encoding does not check that the agreement is between the right parties; it takes that as given.)
GIVEN `exists` IS A BOOLEAN, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `made on or after 21 November 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement displaces the default` IF
        `exists`
    AND (`in writing` OR (NOT `made on or after 21 November 2021`))

GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is an effective contrary agreement` IF
    `the agreement displaces the default` (m's `a contrary agreement exists`) (m's `the agreement is in writing`) (m's `the agreement was made on or after 21 November 2021`)

§§ `136(1)(a), (d) -- the Government`

-- s 136(1): "Despite subsections (3) and (4) and sections 133, 134 and 135, the Government is the first owner of -- (a) any copyright
-- in an unpublished authorial work made by or under the direction or control of the Government (including any copyright in the
-- work after it is published); ... (d) any copyright in a sound recording or film, if the recording or film is made or first
-- published by or under the direction or control of the Government."
-- Only paras (a) and (d), and for (d) only "made", are encoded.
GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 136 makes the Government first owner` IF
        m's `made by or under the direction or control of the Government`
    AND (    (`is an authorial work` (m's `the kind of work`) AND m's `still unpublished when made`)
          OR m's `the kind of work` EQUALS `sound recording`
          OR m's `the kind of work` EQUALS `film`)

§§ `134 -- works made in the course of employment`

-- s 134(1): "This section applies where, in the course of a contract of service, the employee -- (a) makes an authorial work; or
-- (b) does any of the following on or after 21 November 2021: (i) makes a sound recording, film or broadcast; (ii) provides a cable
-- programme service in which a cable programme is included; (iii) publishes an edition of an authorial work."
-- (2): the first owner "is to be determined according to this section (and not section 133)".
GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 134 applies` IF
        m's `made by an employee in the course of a contract of service`
    AND (`is an authorial work` (m's `the kind of work`) OR m's `made on or after 21 November 2021`)

-- s 134(4): "Where -- (a) the relevant work is a literary work, a dramatic work or an artistic work; (b) the employer is the
-- proprietor of a periodical; and (c) the work is made for publication in a periodical". A musical work is NOT in the list. A
-- computer program is a literary work (s 13(1)(b)), so in principle it is in the list.
GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the periodical rule applies` IF
        (    `is a literary work` (m's `the kind of work`)
          OR m's `the kind of work` EQUALS `dramatic work`
          OR m's `the kind of work` EQUALS `artistic work`)
    AND m's `the employer is the proprietor of a periodical`
    AND m's `made for publication in a periodical`

§§ `133 -- the default first owner`

-- s 133(1): "the first owner of copyright in a work is -- (a) in the case of an authorial work -- subject to subsection (2), the
-- author; (b) in the case of a published edition of an authorial work -- the publisher; (c) in the case of a sound recording -- the
-- maker of the recording; (d) in the case of a film -- the maker of the film; (e) in the case of a broadcast -- the broadcasting
-- licensee that made the broadcast; and (f) in the case of a cable programme -- the person providing the cable programme service".
DECLARE Owner IS ONE OF
    `the author`
    `the publisher`
    `the maker`
    `the broadcasting licensee`
    `the cable programme service provider`
    `the employer`
    `the employer, but the employee may restrain publication other than in a periodical`
    `the employer for periodical publication only, the employee for everything else`
    `the Government`
    `whoever the contrary agreement names`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind
GIVETH AN Owner
`the default first owner of` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `published edition` THEN `the publisher`
    WHEN `sound recording` THEN `the maker`
    WHEN `film` THEN `the maker`
    WHEN `broadcast` THEN `the broadcasting licensee`
    WHEN `cable programme` THEN `the cable programme service provider`
    OTHERWISE `the author`

§§ `133 to 136 -- the first owner`

-- s 134(3): "Subject to subsection (4), the employer is the first owner of any copyright in the relevant work."
-- s 134(4), where it applies: "(d) if the work is made on or after 10 April 1987 -- (i) the employer is the first owner of any
-- copyright in the work only to the extent that the copyright relates to -- (A) publishing the work in any periodical; or (B) making
-- a copy of the work for the purpose of its being so published; and (ii) the employee is otherwise the first owner ...; and (e) if
-- the work was made before 10 April 1987, the employee is entitled to restrain the publication of the work otherwise than in a
-- periodical."
-- Order of the tests: the Government first (s 136(1) applies "despite" ss 133 to 135, and is displaced only by its own agreement under
-- s 136(2)); then a contrary agreement (ss 133(3), 134(5)); then s 134; then s 133.
GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH AN Owner
`the first owner of copyright` m MEANS
    IF `section 136 makes the Government first owner` m AND (NOT `there is an effective contrary agreement` m)
    THEN `the Government`
    ELSE IF `there is an effective contrary agreement` m
         THEN `whoever the contrary agreement names`
         ELSE IF `section 134 applies` m
              THEN IF `the periodical rule applies` m
                   THEN IF m's `made on or after 10 April 1987`
                        THEN `the employer for periodical publication only, the employee for everything else`
                        ELSE `the employer, but the employee may restrain publication other than in a periodical`
                   ELSE `the employer`
              ELSE `the default first owner of` (m's `the kind of work`)

GIVEN m IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer owns the whole copyright` IF
    `the first owner of copyright` m EQUALS `the employer`
